From: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: core: never fetch configuration/interface strings

Set USB_QUIRK_CONFIG_INTF_STRINGS on every device so usb_set_configuration()
and usb_create_sysfs_intf_files() skip the iConfiguration/iInterface string
reads. Those strings only populate the sysfs `configuration` and `interface`
attributes, which nothing on this appliance reads: usb-proxy mirrors the raw
descriptors and forwards the host's own string requests to the device live.

Why it matters here: the Moto 360 (minnow) fastboot bootloader, 22b8:42d1,
names a configuration string (iConfiguration=4) that it never answers.
usb_set_configuration() fetches it while holding the device lock, so the
kernel sat in the 5 s USB_CTRL_GET_TIMEOUT (usb_string_sub can retry with a
2-byte read, so up to 10 s per index) and usb-proxy's usbfs open() blocked
behind the lock. Measured on the appliance 2026-09-08: "device found" to
"opened" 5.0 s for the bootloader versus 1.0 s (the settle debounce) for
Android; fastboot became visible on the Mac 5.5 s after the kernel's
enumeration line. With the quirk, 1.0 s and ~1.2 s. A Mac never asks for
that string, which is why a direct connection never paid it.

The OR sits before the dynamic quirks, whose XOR semantics let
usbcore.quirks=VID:PID:d (or a runtime write to
/sys/module/usbcore/parameters/quirks) switch the skip back off for one
device, should any device ever need those strings cached.

Signed-off-by: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/core/quirks.c b/drivers/usb/core/quirks.c
index 6926bd639..3555ba9e0 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/core/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/quirks.c
@@ -717,6 +717,17 @@ void usb_detect_quirks(struct usb_device *udev)
 		udev->quirks |= usb_detect_static_quirks(udev,
 				usb_amd_resume_quirk_list);
 
+	/*
+	 * Appliance: the configuration and interface strings only populate
+	 * sysfs, which nothing here reads, and fetching them costs up to
+	 * 2 x USB_CTRL_GET_TIMEOUT per index on a device that never answers
+	 * (the minnow fastboot bootloader: 5 s with the device lock held, so
+	 * usbfs open() blocked behind it). Skip them for every device. This
+	 * sits before the dynamic quirks, whose XOR lets usbcore.quirks=VID:PID:d
+	 * switch it back off for one device.
+	 */
+	udev->quirks |= USB_QUIRK_CONFIG_INTF_STRINGS;
+
 	udev->quirks ^= usb_detect_dynamic_quirks(udev);
 
 	if (udev->quirks)
